Description: Size the module-file name buffer from its inputs to prevent a heap overflow
 modfile_name() expands the -m/-s format into a fixed MODFILE_NAME_LEN (256)
 byte heap buffer with no bound.  A module name, submodule name or source path
 longer than about 255 characters (the default format is "%f.o", so a long
 source path is enough), or a long -m/-s format, writes past the buffer.
 Reproduced with AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow write at
 modfile_name.c, modfile_name.
 .
 The buffer is now allocated with room for every format character expanding to
 the longest of the three names, so no name is truncated.  Output is unchanged.
Author: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1155613
Forwarded: https://bugs.debian.org/1155613
